    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d713">

                <pb facs="0755" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg743"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.85/772: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-10-01T11:00:00-03:00">October 1, 1942—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received noon.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3923. Ship deal officially consummated today with the exchange of notes between
                    Aranha and myself.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d713-f1"/> Brazilians say that there
                    will be no publicity here.</p>
                <p>I will telegraph later regarding commodity transactions.</p>
                <p>Please send surveyors requested in my 3787, September 23, 6 p.m.<anchor n="30"
                        xml:id="d713-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d713-f1" n="29" xml:id="d713-f1-content">
                <p>Copies of the notes and the charter were transmitted to the Department by the
                    Ambassador in his despatch No. 8629, October 1, 1942, not printed. The agreement
                    of September 30 provided for the chartering by the United States Government of
                    13 vessels owned by the Brazilian Government and the placing under the
                    protection of American convoys 23 other ships flying the Brazilian flag.
                    Provisions were included concerning the increase in the number of ships in the
                    Brazilian-American trade, the loss of ships and compensation therefor,
                    recruiting of personnel, etc. (800.85/775)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d713-f2" n="30" xml:id="d713-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
